        "tsinghua-cbicr": { "why": "Builds brain-inspired computing theory, chips, software, systems, and applications across neuroscience and engineering. Based at Tsinghua University in Beijing, China, this center is distinctive for connecting neuromorphic, brain-inspired AI, and chips within one research effort.", "methods": "Primary approaches: Neuromorphic; Brain-inspired AI; Chips. Linked tools and modalities: Neuromorphic neural coprocessors (spikes / biomarkers -> low-power inference; implant or wearable edge compute); Adaptive neural decoders (population activity -> latent intent / state; task-dependent); Multiscale circuit models and digital twins (anatomy + physiology + behavior -> simulation; ion channel to whole-brain network).", "evidenceLabel": "Official center or institutional page — Center for Brain-Inspired Computing Research (cbicr.tsinghua.edu.cn)" },
