        "kaist-binp": { "why": "Studies neural responses to electrical, magnetic, thermal, and acoustic stimulation while developing next-generation prosthetic devices. Based at KAIST in Daejeon, South Korea, this lab is distinctive for connecting neural stimulation, prostheses, and mechanisms within one research effort.", "methods": "Primary approaches: Neural stimulation; Prostheses; Mechanisms. Linked tools and modalities: Intracortical microstimulation (microampere-scale cortical pulses; local cortical populations); Optogenetics (light-gated cell activity; cell-type / projection specificity); Magnetothermal neuromodulation (magnetic nanoparticle heating; injected target volume / cell type).", "evidenceLabel": "Official lab or institutional page — Brain Interfaces and Neuronal Prosthetics Lab (binp.kaist.ac.kr)" },
