        "navifus": { "why": "NaviFUS is included for its work across neuronavigated focused ultrasound, blood-brain-barrier opening, and epilepsy therapy. Its role is to shorten the loop between detecting abnormal neural activity and delivering or guiding a targeted response.", "methods": "Develops a neuronavigation-guided focused-ultrasound platform for targeted blood-brain-barrier opening and neuromodulation in CNS disease. The linked technology anchors are Functional ultrasound imaging, Low-intensity focused ultrasound, and Adaptive neural decoders. The atlas groups the operating approach under neuronavigated focused ultrasound, blood-brain-barrier opening, and epilepsy therapy; these links show the adjacent sensing, stimulation, decoding, rehabilitation, or computing methods rather than implying that every linked method is one product.", "evidenceLabel": "NaviFUS — official website" },
        "brain-navi": { "why": "Brain Navi Biotechnology is included for its work across neurosurgical robotics, stereotactic navigation, and brain biopsy. Its role is translating a defined stimulation target and dosing workflow into a practical neuromodulation platform for therapy or investigation.", "methods": "Develops NaoTrac, an autonomous stereotactic navigation robot for precise cranial biopsy and other neurosurgical procedures. The linked technology anchors are sEEG depth electrodes, Deep brain stimulation, and Adaptive neural decoders. The atlas groups the operating approach under neurosurgical robotics, stereotactic navigation, and brain biopsy; these links show the adjacent sensing, stimulation, decoding, rehabilitation, or computing methods rather than implying that every linked method is one product.", "evidenceLabel": "Brain Navi Biotechnology — official website" },
